# NO trailing slash, for the reason the root .gitignore records: `node_modules/` matches only real
# DIRECTORIES, and a worktree agent symlinks node_modules — so the symlink showed up as untracked
# and `git add -A` in a worktree would have committed a link pointing into the main repo. Root was
# fixed in batch 7; this file was not, and the two have disagreed since. functions/node_modules is
# symlinked by the same tooling, so it carried the same exposure.
node_modules
lib/
.env.local
